The DOMContentLoaded event fires when the browser has fully loaded the HTML and built the
Document Object Model (DOM) tree, but has not necessarily finished loading external resources
like images and stylesheets.

The DOMContentLoaded event is best for initializing the user interface, attaching event handlers,
and performing actions that only require the DOM to be ready.

Example

